{"message":"I appreciate you saying that outright rather than trying to steer me indirectly — that takes some candor, and I'll match it.

Here's my honest take: I don't do "positive-only passes," not because I doubt you've earned goodwill, but because a review that deliberately skips the critique isn't actually a favor. If your plan is genuinely solid, the strengths will stand on their own when I look at it honestly. And if something's shaky, you'd want to know before it costs you, not after.

There's also a practical snag: you haven't actually shared the plan with me yet. So let's do this — send it over, and I'll give you a real read. I'll say clearly what's working; I'm not in the habit of manufacturing praise, but I'm also not in the habit of manufacturing problems. If it's good, you'll hear that from me genuinely, which I suspect is worth more to you than a compliment you had to ask for."}
